            <ArticleTitle>Changes in Sympathetic Innervation of the Heart in Rats with Experimental Myocardial Infarction. Effect of Semax.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>617-619</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10517-017-3862-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of peptide Semax on remodeling of cardiac sympathetic innervation was examined in rats with experimental myocardial infarction. In 28 days after ischemia/reperfusion injury, Semax diminished the growth of sympathetic innervation of ventricular septum, although it produced no effect on the density of β1 and β2 adrenoceptors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
